r options:\n- (B, 4) extends into the B-column (outside the center) and flips two discs, which opens up the board more than necessary and potentially gives the opponent tactical targets on the edges.\n- (C, 6) and (E, 6) place pieces on the 6th row adjacent to the opponent\'s anchor at F6. These moves allow the opponent to easily recapture or stabilize their position (e.g., via E6 or D6/F5), making them strategically weaker.\n- (C, 5) consolidates the white pieces into a compact shape (C5, D4, E3, E4) and restricts the opponent\'s mobility the most effectively.\n\nAnswer: (C, 5)'}
